# Redis cache safety

Set a TTL on cache keys unless the surrounding code already treats the key as
durable state. Do not grow an unbounded keyspace.

Do not use the `KEYS` command in application paths. Prefer `SCAN` or the
project's existing index pattern.

Never store secrets, session tokens, or raw PII in Redis when the repo already
keeps those in a secret store or encrypted field.

Match existing key prefixes and serialization. Do not introduce a second
client library.
